RF.put("questb:b17",{"8657":{"id":8657,"t":"Striker's Diadem","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'lor's Diadem Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Strife Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will make you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nStriker's Diadem\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8657\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Striker's Diadem this quest\nBring Vek'lor's Diadem, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"98417":{"id":98417,"t":"Vengeful trail","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maseara Autumnmoon wants you to search west of Forest Song, amongst the Satyrnaar demons. Report any signs of her husband Kurothel upon your return.\nVine-Wrapped Scroll","desc":"At the moment our fates bound us most vulnerable, tragedy fell upon our villages. Satyrs defiled our temples, their profane touch staining sacred boughs, and they slaughtered the innocent without mercy.\nKurothel was consumed by wrath. The druids are taking the fight to the satyr, and he has followed.\nOur bond endures. I feel my husband, west, within these woods. Please, return to me with news of his fate.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":81,"y":50.2,"n":"Maseara Autumnmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"737":{"id":737,"t":"Forbidden Knowledge","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Yagyin's Digest to Theldurin.\nYagyin's Digest\nProvided: Yagyin's Digest","desc":"I have the digest for you, ‹name›. I need not tell you to take great care with it. And to keep it far from unfriendly hands.\nThis book holds many truths...\n...And the truth can burn.","rew":"You will receive:\nSkull of Impending Doom\nExperience: 2,350","back":"Ho! You were gone a long time. Did you get the digest?","done":"You got it! Oh, hope glimmers!\nYour efforts may yet save us, ‹name›. A monument they should make of you! A shrine they should build! May your name be praised until your grandchildren have grandchildren!\nUnless...THEY are freed and rise to the surface. If that happens then you can forget about children.\nIf THEY are freed, then we're all worm food.\nDun Morogh Undercity Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":53.7,"y":54.5,"n":"Keeper Bel'dugur","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97937":{"id":97937,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Vhan in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94337":{"id":94337,"t":"Craftsmans writ gnomish alarm o bot","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Gnomish Alarm-O-Bot\nGnomish Alarm-O-Bot","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Gnomish Alarm-O-Bot, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Gnomish Alarm-O-Bot Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94337","cats":["crafting"]},"94257":{"id":94257,"t":"Craftsmans writ lesser invisibility potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Lesser Invisibility Potion\nLesser Invisibility Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Lesser Invisibility Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Lesser Invisibility Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94257","cats":["crafting"]},"7937":{"id":7937,"t":"Your Fortune Awaits You...","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest and seek out your fortune.\nSayge's Fortune #23\nProvided: Sayge's Fortune #23","desc":"\"Your fortune awaits you in Eastvale.\"\nThe fortune Sayge handed you feels slightly warm to the touch. Grasping it firmly, you see an image of the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest. Focusing closer in on the image, you see a haystack that sits next to a stable.","rew":"You will receive:\nMysterious Lockbox\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"This haystack looks like the one from your vision.","done":"A quick search of the haystack reveals a lockbox from within it! It would seem that you have found your fortune!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.9,"y":64.4,"n":"Mysterious Eastvale Haystack","e":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"98897":{"id":98897,"t":"Darkspear islands clash","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle against the Darkspear Raiders is heating up. Without urgent aid, the Darkspear Islands will be lost to us.\nIt is your duty as a proud member of the Alliance to ensure this does not happen. Bring me proof of your contributions on the front lines and you will be revered as a hero of the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper\n+150 reputation with Theramore Expeditionary Force\nLevel 49 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 45 47 52 60 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 98897","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"92817":{"id":92817,"t":"Leather technique","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Barbaric Harness to Talra in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nBarbaric Harness\nGelkis Clan Centaur:","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPattern: Mystic Thick Armor Kit Pattern: Blue Suede Armor\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+1,000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Quest ID 92817","cats":["desolace"]},"1457":{"id":1457,"t":"The Karnitol Shipwreck","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,250 experience instead of 1,500, 1.5 times as much.","obj":"Bring Karnitol's Satchel to Roetten Stonehammer in Ironforge.\nKarnitol's Satchel Slitherblade Sea Witch 20 % , Slitherblade Tidehunter 20 %\nProvided: Karnitol's Satchel","desc":"Take Karnitol's things back to Roetten in Ironforge and he'll pay you for a job well done.\nHaha, if you're not careful, he's gonna be so pleased with ya that he'll ask you to join us full time.\nAgain, great job, ‹name›.\nBe careful on your way back, and don't take too much time--Karnitol's not the most of patient of men, but he's very generous nonetheless.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHellion Boots Sanguine Pauldrons\nExperience: 2,250\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Business is booming, ‹name›, and I don't have a lot of time for questions. If you've got business with the Reclaimers, then let's hear it. If not, I'm gonna have to ask you to talk to one of me underlings - they're adept enough at taking care of things 'round here.","done":"Ah, the Karnitol business in Desolace. Excellent!\nSo, the chest was destroyed, but the items are all here, huh? Well, I'll let him be the judge of that. One good part about this business I got going on here is that if they're not satisfied, I can tell 'em to shove it! They're relyin' on us to find their stuff... not make sure it's all pretty and in good shape when they get it back.\nGood work, ‹name›. Let's see about gettin' you paid.\nDesolace Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.5,"n":"Roetten Stonehammer","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"95217":{"id":95217,"t":"The quarrys smith","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 12 Copper Bars and 4 Toughened Boar Hides and deliver them to Frast Dokner.\n12 Copper Bar\n4 Toughened Boar Hide","desc":"So you're looking to learn the blacksmith's trade? Maybe we can help each other.\nThe supply shipment's late, and I need materials for some repairs around the camp. If you get me what I need, I'll teach you some of my techniques. Sound fair?","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Rough Copper Chain Boots\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Don't slack off, ‹name›. Smithin' isn't for the lazy!","done":"You're a resourceful one, ‹name›.\nNow listen up - I'm not going to repeat myself!\nDun Morogh The Barrens Westfall Silverpine Forest Redridge Mountains Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":68.8,"y":55.8,"n":"Frast Dokner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"417":{"id":417,"t":"A Pilot's Revenge","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Mangeclaw.\nBring his Mangy Claw and Hildelve's Journal to Pilot Hammerfoot.\nMangy Claw Mangeclaw\nHildelve's Journal\nProvided: Hildelve's Journal","desc":"Hildelve wrote in his journal that he was attacked by Mangeclaw, a \"huge Ice Claw Bear.\" He drove off the beast, but not before it mauled him savagely.\nJudging from the state of Hildelve's body, Mangeclaw must have later returned and killed him.\nHowever, Hildelve wrote in his journal his one, final wish:\nRevenge against Mangeclaw.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCraftsman's Dagger Compact Hammer\nExperience: 650\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Do you have word of my friend Hildelve?","done":"This is grim news, for Hildelve was a good friend. And I wish I could have been there with you when you found the beast, Mangeclaw!\nThank you, ‹name›. Your deed will be remembered by the pilots of the Ironforge Siege Brigade.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":79.7,"y":36.2,"n":"A Dwarven Corpse","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":83.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Pilot Hammerfoot","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"817":{"id":817,"t":"Practical Prey","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Durotar Tiger Furs to Vel'rin Fang in Sen'jin Village.\n4 Durotar Tiger Fur Durotar Tiger 35 %","desc":"Many of the hides we use come from Durotar tigers, ‹name›. Blankets, armor, tents: there are a great many reasons we hunt the beasts, and many reasons we let them thrive at the same time.\nThe time has come for us to cull the flock, so to speak. Our numbers grow, and our needs are beginning to overwhelm our stocks. I need more hides if I'm to prepare suitable goods for our people.\nBring me 4 Durotar tiger furs, and I shall reward you. You can find them on the islands south of here.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I remember my first tiger hunt, ‹name›. I chose to hunt on the largest of the Echo Isles, and I sat perfectly still in the shadows of its foliage for almost a full day... watching... waiting.\nMy muscles were taut, and I was ready to strike. It was one of my greatest victories when that tiger finally took the bait.","done":"I am pleased, ‹name›. Because of your help, our people will be protected, and not go cold as the seasons change.\nThank you.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":56,"y":73.9,"n":"Vel'rin Fang","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"337":{"id":337,"t":"An Old History Book","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the book: The History of Stormwind, to the Stormwind Library.\nAn Old History Book Gutspill 1 % , Splinter Fist Enslaver 1 % , Fetid Corpse 1 % , Splinter Fist Firemonger 1 % and 4 more\nProvided: An Old History Book","desc":"Although the cover of this book is marred by scratches and caked with mud, the words \"The History of Stormwind\" can still be read along its spine. Upon opening the book, the seal of the Stormwind Library is clearly stamped on the book's first page.\nIt looks like someone checked out this book, and never returned it...","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,500\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ooh! What's that old book you have there? Can I see it??","done":"Oh my! This book hasn't rested on these shelves since before the rebuilding of Stormwind, years ago. It will have to be restored of course, it's in bad shape, but I would be honored to place it within our rare books collection.\nThank you, ‹name›. Please accept this as payment for returning the book!\nStormwind City Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":30.2,"n":"Milton Sheaf","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"177":{"id":177,"t":"Look To The Stars","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Look To The Stars.","obj":"Retrieve Blind Mary's Looking Glass from the Insane Ghoul and give it to Viktori in Darkshire.\nMary's Looking Glass Insane Ghoul","desc":"The looking glass was one of my finest treasures until. . .the incident. After that happened, I discarded it behind the barn. There was an Insane Ghoul who used to roam back there. Perhaps he picked it up. Rumor has it the devilish beast resides in the Tranquil Gardens Cemetery.","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I showed Cog the beginnings of our star-viewing machine. He was impressed. Did you happen to find a reflective device?","done":"Most superb! This will work perfectly. Many thanks!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":82,"y":59.1,"n":"Blind Mary","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":79.8,"y":48,"n":"Viktori Prism'Antras","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"97":{"id":97,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report the news to Commander Ebonlocke.","desc":"Let Commander Ebonlocke know immediately that the handwriting matched, ‹name›! Her suspicions were correct!","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes, ‹name›?","done":"I knew it! Fine work, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9137":{"id":9137,"t":"Savage Fronds","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Savage Frond Razorlash 54 % , Bloodpetal Trapper 46.5 % , Bloodpetal Lasher 44.8 % , Bloodpetal Flayer 44.6 % and 4 more","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Dawn Insignia of the Crusade\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"For every bundle of fronds that you deliver to me, I will pay you with your choice of an insignia of the Dawn or the Crusade.\nInsignias may be turned in to the Quartermaster for various rewards.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Your work is vital to the success of our campaign against the Scourge.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91777":{"id":91777,"t":"Rare books","lv":7,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\" and return them to Brother Paxton inside Northshire's Abbey.\nGeomancy for Curious Young Wizards\nArcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words","desc":"There's just two books left missing on Brother Paxton's list: \"Geomancy for Curious Young Wizards\" and \"Arcane Explainer: Magical Stuff in Simple Words\".\nThe kobolds must have taken them to the Jasperlode Mine. Please track down those two books and bring them back to Brother Paxton.\nBut I'm afraid it will be quite dangerous. If the \"apprentice\" kobold was summoning an elemental, who knows what the master can do. I'd bring some friends if I were you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nApprentice's Spellstaff Militia Shortblade Militia Sword Northshire Hammer Militia Bow\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 800\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you found all my missing books yet?","done":"Oh, Critopher! Thank you so much for saving my library. You've done me an amazing service. Please take one of these fine weapons. They were intended for the militia, but you can make better use of them.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.2,"y":65.8,"n":"Marshal Dughan","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Brother Paxton","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"95697":{"id":95697,"t":"Changing tastes","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Enter the Excavation Sites in the Wetlands and bring back Thicket Raptor Meat.\n4 Thicket Raptor Meat","desc":"Zamja tells me we need more homestyle cooking.\nIf we start selling raptor, she thinks it'll draw in customers who don't usually visit Borstan's Firepit.\nHer idea is not so bad. But I want something that rises above the smells of our birth villages. We're in Orgrimmar! Borstan should serve a grand take on their familiar favorites.\nA hunter recently came back from the Wetlands with a giant talon from the thicket raptors in the Excavation Sites.\nUp for a job?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSatchel of Potions Serrated Raptor Claw\nYou will also receive:\nRecipe: Twice-Spiced Raptor Slice 5 Twice-Spiced Raptor Slice\nExperience: 6,950","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":57.4,"y":53.4,"n":"Borstan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"657":{"id":657,"t":"Hints of a New Plague?","lv":36,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Kinelory.","desc":"<Quae begins to go through the folder.>\nThis IS interesting. Seems Apothecary Jorell has been working on some deadly experiments here at Go'Shek. Not sure what that has to do with Hillsbrad, but Phin wouldn't like it if we let it continue.\nWe had a run-in with some orcs while you were gone, and I'm not in good enough shape to help Kinelory. If you're up for it, she's going to need some protection when she goes down to the farm to steal whatever research Jorell still hasn't sent to Tarren Mill.","done":"If it brings Phin peace, I'll destroy every single one of the Forsaken personally. He's done so much for us since the plague. We never thought we'd find friends or family again.\nWhen you're prepared, come let me know. We'll get started right away.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.8,"n":"Quae","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":60.2,"y":53.9,"n":"Kinelory","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"2977":{"id":2977,"t":"Return to Ironforge","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Historian Karnik in Ironforge.\nMiniature Platinum Discs\nProvided: Miniature Platinum Discs","desc":"You access the pedestal again; the platinum discs suddenly appear once more in your backpack.\nWith the knowledge of the stone watcher learned and the discs returned to your possession, the time has come to return to Ironforge and inform the Explorers' League of your discovery.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Welcome back ‹name›. Were you able to use the discs to your advantage, or did it end up being a wild goose chase?","done":"You were missing some discs? Interestingly enough, it seems that the discs of Norgannon are only parts of the complete set - like keys on a key ring, if you will.\nIf we can find the Plates of Uldum, then we could actually access the Uldum complex itself! Imagine actually exploring the place where the Creators worked without having to bring a huge shovel!\nNot that there's anything wrong with shovels... or digging...\nTanaris Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":37.6,"y":81.4,"n":"Uldum Pedestal","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8977":{"id":8977,"t":"Return to Deliana","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer to Deliana in Ironforge.\nExtra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer\nProvided: Extra-Dimensional Ghost Revealer","desc":"It's been great working with you, ‹name›. Here is the finished product.\nI hope it helps you in your current endeavors. And hey, if you don't mind, help spread the word. I wouldn't mind having more customers!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"You've returned?","done":"Excellent! You've done well, ‹name›. I'm not sure I trust the goblin's craftsmanship, but I'm left with no other choice.\nTanaris Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Mux Manascrambler","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"257":{"id":257,"t":"A Hunter's Boast","lv":16,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Mountain Buzzards and return to Daryl the Youngling in the Farstrider Lodge within 15 minutes.\nMountain Buzzard slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Think you can match wits with Daryl the Bold, huh? I should think not! Of course, you're more than welcome to try. Here's a challenge that should prove to be above your abilities, so don't feel too bad if you can't face up to it.\nA flock of buzzards has nested here in Loch Modan. Why don't you try to take down some of the beasts? Tell you what, if you meet my challenge in fifteen minutes, I'll give you my bow or gun.\n<He looks you over dismissively.>\nIt seems you haven't much to lose, anyways.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDaryl's Hunting Bow Daryl's Hunting Rifle\nExperience: 875","back":"No luck? Don't feel too bad, ‹name›...\nNot everyone can be me.","done":"What? Success?\nTake it from me, ‹name›ama, you don't let it get to your head. I mean, any unshaven boy with a bow could have killed such... small specimens. And I hope you don't enjoy killing the buzzards so much, yes? We wouldn't want them to become extinct.\nWell, err... Never let it be said that Daryl the Bold would not hold to his word.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":83.5,"y":65.5,"n":"Daryl the Youngling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"98977":{"id":98977,"t":"Mossheart the elder","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 98977","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9057":{"id":9057,"t":"Cryptstalker Spaulders","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Huntsman Leopold at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Cryptstalker Spaulders if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Spaulders, 12 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Spaulders Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I have discovered a use for the carapace of the crypt fiend. I am able to fashion an extremely light and very deadly set of armor by combining the fragments with some of the desecrated magical armors lost in Naxxramas.\nBring me the items I require and I shall fashion for you a suit of armor the likes of which has never before been seen in our world!","rew":"You will receive:\nCryptstalker Spaulders\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Cryptstalker Spaulders.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"94817":{"id":94817,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","done":"You took your time arriving, ‹name›. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":24.8,"y":10,"n":"High Priestess Mims","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8257":{"id":8257,"t":"Blood of Morphaz","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Morphaz in the sunken temple of Atal'Hakkar, and return his blood to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood. The entrance to the sunken temple can be found in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nBlood of Morphaz Morphaz","desc":"Now the last part, the second cure.\nThe green drake Morphaz is known to be immune to all forms of poison and disease -- many druids died to bring us this information. There is no doubt his blood is potent for our needs.\nA courier from the Cenarion Circle will take the parts you have already collected while you gather the last. Summon your allies and seek out the drake's lair in the sunken temple of Atal'Hakkar. Bring his blood to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlessed Prayer Beads Woestave Circle of Hope\nMoney: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350","back":"Do you have the blood of Morphaz?","done":"You have slain Morphaz and carried his blood to us... I can hardly believe this good news!\nWe will combine the ingredients at once and begin healing the trees and creatures of Felwood. It will take a lifetime to undo what has happened here, but you have given us the means to do it.\nAzshara Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":42.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Ogtinc","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8817":{"id":8817,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Horde Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Thunder Bluff.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":30.4,"y":65.6,"n":"Undercity Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.4,"y":57,"n":"Officer Thunderstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"3377":{"id":3377,"t":"Prayer to Elune","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hear Zamael tell his tale.","desc":"Will you assist me, mortal? Hear my tale.","rew":"Experience: 470","back":"Allow me to finish my story.","done":"I have accepted my fate here in this cage, but the prayer must be found.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":29.6,"y":26.3,"n":"Zamael Lunthistle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8897":{"id":8897,"t":"Dearest Colara,","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Lieutenant Heldric's Carefully Penned Note to Colara Dean outside the bank in Stormwind.\nCarefully Penned Note\nProvided: Carefully Penned Note","desc":"I've got to keep watch here at the gate, but I'm always worrying about my sweetheart, Colara. I only get to see her for a few hours, if I'm lucky, and well, just look at me. I've got a minor officer's pay and I could be called to the front any day now.\nWould she just forget about me? There are a lot of men in the city. A lot of rich ones.\nAnyways, I've scribbled some things down... nothing much, but if you could take it to her for me, that'd be great.","back":"Hello there, handsome. Something I can help you with?","done":"Oh, isn't that sweet! This is the first time he's ever sent me something. Do you suppose he's getting serious?\nColara Heldric? I suppose it has a ring to it. Oh, but I'm getting ahead of myself. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":63.8,"y":70.6,"n":"Lieutenant Jocryn Heldric","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.7,"y":75.5,"n":"Colara Dean","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94497":{"id":94497,"t":"Call of water","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the bottom of the waterfalls below Hervdana's cave and return it to her in the Wetlands.\nFull Brown Waterskin","desc":"Ah, so ye've come seekin' the sapta, have ye? Well then, listen close, love. To find understandin' and earn the sapta, ye must seek water in its various forms. As ye gather the samples, keep yer eyes open. Watch the beasts that guard it, the land it nourishes, and how it changes lives.\nWe'll start simple: fill this skin at the base o' the falls, where the fresh meets the brackish. Go on now, and mind the marsh.","back":"I'm nearly ready to send ye off on the rest o' yer tasks. But tell me, have ye filled the skin yet? The ocean brings life, aye -- but it carries sediment, minerals, and energies far different from the snowmelt and springwater of the highlands. Where sea and spring meet, there's wisdom to be found.","done":"Glad ye managed to steer clear o' the Dark Iron. Shame they've crept so far north--makes ye wonder what dwarfkind could do if the clans ever stopped squabblin' and worked as one.\nStill, the tides rise high when the moons are strong, and the seawater floods the marsh. It's here that we study our estuary water.\nThank ye for this sacred offering, it marks the beginning of your stage as a vessel--one who seeks the waters' wisdom.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":65.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Hervdana Saegrund","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8737":{"id":8737,"t":"Azure Templar","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Summon and slay an Azure Templar and report back to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\nTactical Task Briefing I\nAzure Templar slain\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing I","desc":"The Twilight's Hammer and the elemental nobles they worship present a formidable threat to our operations in Silithus. With the new enemies we're facing inside Ahn'Qiraj, we cannot afford to lower our guard to our enemies outside.\nFind a way to summon and destroy an Azure Templar and report to Bor Wildmane.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Followup Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Is your task done yet, ‹name›?","done":"Good job, ‹name›. Here's your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8497":{"id":8497,"t":"Desert Survival Kits","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Globes of Water, 4 Powerful Anti-Venom and 4 Smoked Desert Dumplings to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\n4 Globe of Water Princess Tempestria 77.1 % , Lord Skwol 47.6 % , Hydrospawn 20 % , Muck Splash 16.1 % and 4 more\n4 Powerful Anti-Venom\n4 Smoked Desert Dumplings\nLogistics Task Briefing I\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing I","desc":"With the arrival of fresh recruits to Cenarion Hold comes the problem of keeping them alive in the desert. Dehydration as well as numerous poisonous creatures present a serious threat to inexperienced volunteers. Gather the supplies necessary for a desert survival kit and bring them to Calandrath in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":39.2,"n":"Calandrath","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1057":{"id":1057,"t":"Reclaiming the Charred Vale","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Keeper Albagorm on Stonetalon Peak wants you to slay 6 Bloodfury Harpies, 6 Bloodfury Ambushers, 6 Bloodfury Slayers and 6 Bloodfury Roguefeathers.\nBloodfury Harpy slain : 0/ 6\nBloodfury Ambusher slain : 0/ 6\nBloodfury Slayer slain : 0/ 6\nBloodfury Roguefeather slain : 0/ 6","desc":"As a protector of the forest spirits you can undoubtedly guess why I am alarmed.\nYou have traveled through these mountains to reach this peak. Surely you have seen the travesty which has befallen the land. Greed has led to the destruction of these sacred hills.\nThe Charred Vale to the south was set afire by the greedy mechanized army of industrialists. Worse yet, the Bloodfuries that have encroached on the land refuse us passage in to begin regrowth.\nDrive the wretched harpies out, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"There is much work to be done before the Charred Vale can be restored to the lush forest it once was.\nClear the area of those foul menaces, ‹name›! Only then can we begin to reclaim what belongs to nature.","done":"Now that the Bloodfuries have suffered such a great loss, perhaps the true work of restoring the land can begin....","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":37.1,"y":8.1,"n":"Keeper Albagorm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"577":{"id":577,"t":"Some Assembly Required","lv":36,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Snapjaw Crocolisks Skins to Drizzlik in Booty Bay.\n5 Snapjaw Crocolisk Skin Snapjaw Crocolisk 30 %","desc":"Well, I've got the basic shape of the boots worked out, and they're coming along fine, but the skins you brought aren't going to be quite enough for the inner layers.\n\"What are we going to do, Drizzlik?\" No doubt the question on your lips, and well, isn't it lucky you're talking to Drizzlik, because he's going to tell you what we're going to do!\nThe inner layers will never really be seen, so we'll just get some of the thicker, cheaper skins from the crocs around Lake Nazferiti to fill the boots out.","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,400\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Drizzlik's Excelsior leather boots, finest workmanship, one-hundred percent high quality saltwater crocilisk skin boots. None finer!\nCan't beat a glowing description like that, can you?\nExcept, maybe, if you have those skins for me?","done":"My boots... they're like sausages, ‹name›. Look great, taste great. I tell you they're filled with nothing but the finest ingredients and meats, and you eat it, and you love it.\nIt's safer--and more enjoyable--if you just trust me, and don't ask too carefully what's really inside.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.3,"y":77.6,"n":"Drizzlik","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8577":{"id":8577,"t":"Stewvul, Ex-B.F.F.","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Narain Soothfancy wants you to find his ex-best friend forever (BFF), Stewvul, and take back the scrying goggles that Stewvul stole from him.","desc":"If I am to translate anything, I will need my scrying goggles. Unfortunately, those were stolen quite some time ago by my ex-best friend forever, Stewvul. He broke my heart in five places and then left me here to rot.\nWith the help of my trusty crystal ball, I've isolated his whereabouts to either the Greymane Wall in Silverpine or what appears to be a portal world in the Outland that is currently being overrun by the Burning Legion. You're going to have to track him down and get my goggles back, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+10 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","done":"I can't believe he found me. I thought for sure that I'd lost him when I was in the Outland. I'm not going back there, ‹race›! No way, no how! I'm through being his part time best friend forever and full time slave.\nTanaris Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.2,"y":18.6,"n":"Narain Soothfancy","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":46.2,"y":86.7,"n":"Inconspicuous Crate","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"897":{"id":897,"t":"The Harvester","lv":24,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Harvester's Head to Jorn Skyseer.\nHarvester's Head Silithid Harvester\nProvided: Harvester's Head","desc":"This strange, insect-like creature looks outside of the natural order, as though it does not belong in the Barrens.","rew":"Experience: 2,400\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"You seemed troubled, ‹name›. How go your lessons in the Barrens? Did you find something that disturbs you?","done":"I can tell nothing of the nature of this beast, for its spirit has fled. But as you guessed, it does not belong in the Barrens. I fear it may herald a grim future for our people...\nBut for now, prepare yourself, and let us hope that time unravels the mystery of this creature.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1137":{"id":1137,"t":"News for Fizzle","lv":38,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Fizzle Brassbolts in the Shimmering Flats.","desc":"Indurium has an amazing resistance to heat! I'm sure it will work for Fizzle's pistons. But he'll need true indurium ore, not just the flakes.\nTo get the ore, it must be mined from deep within Uldaman, on the northern borders of the Badlands. That is the true source of indurium.\nSend Fizzle Brassbolts my regards, and tell him what I told you.\nSafe travels, ‹name›. And it won't surprise me if we meet again -- once Fizzle learns of indurium he'll probably send you to Uldaman to acquire it!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFizzle's Zippy Lighter Gnomish Mechanic's Gloves\nExperience: 1,450","done":"‹name›, you're back! You found Martek? You spoke with him? What did he say? Can he help??\nTell me, tell me, tell me!!\nBadlands Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":42.2,"y":52.7,"n":"Martek the Exiled","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Fizzle Brassbolts","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"96897":{"id":96897,"t":"The cult of the damned","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Kill 8 Dark Neophytes and 8 Dark Enforcers in Tirisfal Glades.\nDark Neophyte slain : 0/ 8\nDark Enforcer slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The scourge are a blight on our lands, and their living servants are the worst of them. The people of Tirisfal have enough to deal with between the mindless dead and the Scarlet Crusade. If you wish to do some good, help me put an end to this scum.","done":"Thank you for your aid, ‹class›. If we do not wish to see Lordaeron's history repeat itself, we've got to be vigilant when threats like this spring up.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.8,"y":61,"n":"Hadric Harlson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"17":{"id":17,"t":"Uldaman Reagent Run","lv":42,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 38 instead of 36.","obj":"Bring 12 Magenta Fungus Caps to Ghak Healtouch in Thelsamar.\n12 Magenta Fungus Cap Magenta Cap Clusters , Magenta Cap Clusters","desc":"I've heard about a newly discovered plant called the magenta fungus caps. They grow in clusters at the Uldaman dig site and can be found in the early tunnels and deep within the less-explored areas. I want to study their potential use in alchemy, and that's where you come in.\nFind the magenta cap clusters and bring me a dozen caps. Be warned, the clusters may spew out poison spores if jostled.\nDo this for me, and I'll whip up a batch of one of my famous restorative elixirs for you!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Restorative Potion\nMoney: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you obtained the magenta fungus caps I need for my alchemical work? No caps - no reward!","done":"Well done ‹name›, you've proven your worth once again! The caps will be an interesting study, yon verily!\nAnd now, as promised, enjoy a taste of one of my more potent restorative brews from my personal stock...\nIf you are a skilled alchemist, then perhaps we might have some additional business to conduct. Regardless, I thank you for your assistance!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.1,"y":49.4,"n":"Ghak Healtouch","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"4737":{"id":4737,"t":"In Search of Menara Voidrender","lv":31,"min":31,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Hmph, still you strive to become more powerful. I say it's only time before the corruption and addiction takes hold of you and you become a slave to that which you seek to gain power over.\nPfah! A fool you are! Time will prove me right--nothing else... just time.\nBut it seems that not all agree with Zevrost. It seems Menara would create tools for you to become more powerful and to harness your strength. If you're interested, then go to Ratchet in the Barrens. She is there overlooking the town.","rew":"Experience: 625","done":"Ah, Zevrost sent you. Good. Then word does reach far enough to find future students. This pleases me.\nIt is typical of our kind, ‹name›, to band together, regardless of race. It is especially important since those we deal with most do not discriminate in their malice if we fail to appease them or control them properly.\nI feel you've learned a great many things, and if you are willing, I would help you create tools to compliment your skills.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Zevrost","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"8417":{"id":8417,"t":"A Troubled Spirit","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 52 instead of 50.","obj":"Speak with the Fallen Hero of the Horde at the entrance to the Blasted Lands.","desc":"In the Blasted Lands, there is a troubled spirit who was once a great hero of the horde. A warrior's honor does not die with the body, and it would serve you well to speak with him.","rew":"Experience: 500","back":"Did Stoley cough up my booze?","done":"So, you have come to alleviate my pain. I wish you could simply strike me down, but it is not that simple...\nThunder Bluff Orgrimmar Undercity Dun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":57.2,"y":87.4,"n":"Torm Ragetotem","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Sorek","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":46.9,"y":15.2,"n":"Christoph Walker","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.4,"y":35.6,"n":"Kelv Sternhammer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.6,"y":59.9,"n":"Wu Shen","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58.9,"y":35.3,"n":"Darnath Bladesinger","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5217":{"id":5217,"t":"Return to Chillwind Camp","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Felstone Field Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Felstone Field Bottle\nProvided: Filled Felstone Field Bottle","desc":"You fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's poisonous concoction for a suitable sample to be studied.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 80 0 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+50 reputation with Stormwind\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Welcome back to the relative safety of Chillwind Camp, ‹name›. What progress on the cauldrons do you have to report?","done":"Well done ‹name› - it should take Alchemist Arbington no time at all to analyze this and devise a counter agent to introduce into the cauldron. If we are able to pump out enough of it into the air, we might be able to weaken all the Scourge present here.\nThis will no doubt be an ongoing ordeal; we will need to continually hit these cauldrons and introduce our reagents into their mix. Still, if we can keep it up, we will have a huge advantage over Scourge when the time comes for battle!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":37.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5537":{"id":5537,"t":"Skeletal Fragments","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Skeletal Fragments to Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.\n15 Skeletal Fragments Skeletal Terror 80 % , Skeletal Acolyte 80 % , Skeletal Warlord 80 % , Skeletal Executioner 80 % and 2 more","desc":"The key to Scholomance is called a Skeleton Key. It must be forged from the remains of a skeleton - several actually - and hardened by only the strongest of metals within a suitable mold. A signet of power from a being who naturally can open the portal to Scholomance will make the key ultimately function.\nFirst thing's first though, ‹name›. We'll need skeletal fragments for the key's forging. Skeletons inside Andorhal should yield what we need, but the ones outside the walls might work too.","rew":"Experience: 4,500","back":"As morbid as it sounds, we'll need a decent supply of suitable skeletal fragments to make up the outer layer of the key. They don't call it a Skeleton Key for nothing, you know.","done":"This'll work, ‹name›! My turn now - I will imbue these with a suitable temper that will allow them to survive the intense forging process they will eventually go through.\nThe next step will be to get an appropriate mold for the key. I know a goblin blacksmith in Tanaris that has in the past made molds for similarly macabre items. He works for whom goblins usually work for - the highest bidder.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":83.8,"n":"Alchemist Arbington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"977":{"id":977,"t":"Are We There, Yeti?","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 2 Pristine Yeti Horns for Umi Rumplesnicker in Everlook.\n2 Pristine Yeti Horn Ice Thistle Patriarch 10 % , Ice Thistle Matriarch 10 %","desc":"Now that I have what I need to cover the mechanical moving parts, I only need one other thing. Well, actually two. Two horns!\nThe ice thistle patriarchs and matriarchs have the largest horns, so of course, those are the ones I want. That type of yeti inhabits a cave to the southeast. There are plenty of them there; you shouldn't have any problem finding them.\nRemember, I only want the best looking ones -- no beat up or broken horns, please!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,650\n+75 reputation with Everlook","back":"I've just about finished attaching the fur, ‹name›. Please, hurry back with those horns!","done":"I can't wait to show my friends! Now, just wait a moment while I attach these...\nPerfect!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":60.9,"y":37.6,"n":"Umi Rumplesnicker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5057":{"id":5057,"t":"Past Endeavors","lv":60,"min":53,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Storm Shadowhoof's Marker to Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Before you spoke to me, ‹name›, I had heard of your endeavors... that you had an unyielding desire to prove yourself, that you had an exceptional ability as a ‹class›, and I now know these things to be the truth.\nThose that excel as you do are worthy of recognition. Take this marker to a friend of mine in Thunder Bluff named Melor Stonehoof. I'm sure he will remember you, and what you accomplished so long ago. Speak to him of you recent victories, and do not ever forget what you have accomplished today.","rew":"You will receive:\nHunter's Insignia Medal\nExperience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"We learn from our life experiences, ‹name›. From what this marker says, I am sure that you have only become stronger and wiser as a result of yours. You have grown much since we last spoke.\nTake this in remembrance of the difficult tasks you have accomplished as a ‹race› ‹class›, and know that you will always have my respect and admiration.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.4,"n":"Storm Shadowhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94897":{"id":94897,"t":"The fate of a loved one","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find Resaan in the Ruins of Ban'aethal.\nResaan's Heirloom","desc":"If you are traveling to Ban'aethal, I have a selfish request. My love, Resaan... I believe is no longer a part of this world. He had tried to go back to get supplies even though I begged him to stay. It has been over a week already and I fear the worst.\nPlease, if you find him bring him home. If he has perished then I beg you to please bring me his heirloom.","back":"Have you any news of Resaan? Please, ‹class›, the wait is hard to endure after everything that has happened.","done":"<Ealaane's eyes well with tears.>\nOh, Resaan my love. What will become of us now? There was so much... it feels as if our lives together had just started.\nThank you, ‹class›. The world is cruel to take both my home and my love from me. At least his heirloom will give me some closure.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":65.8,"y":74.4,"n":"Ealaane Nimbuswalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});